{title: 598 - Watch, Ye Saints}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C]Watch, ye saints, with eyelids waking;
[G]Lo! the powers of heaven are shaking;
[C]Keep your lamps all trimmed and burning,
Ready for your Lord’s returning.
Lo! [G]He [C]comes, lo! [D]Jesus [G]comes;
[C]Lo! He comes, He comes all glorious!
Jesus comes to reign victorious,
Lo! [G]He [C]comes, [Dm]yes, [G]Jesus [C]comes!

Refrain:
[C]Lo! He comes, lo! Jesus comes;
[G]Lo! He come, He comes all glorious!
[C]Jesus comes to reign victorious,
Lo! He comes, yes, Jesus comes.

Verse 2:
[C]Lo! the promise of your Savior,
[G]Pardoned sin and purchased favor,
[C]Blood-washed robes and crowns of glory;
Haste to tell redemption's story.

Verse 3:
[C]Kingdoms at their base are crumbling,
[G]Hark! His chariot wheels are rumbling;
[C]Tell, O tell of grace abounding,
While the seventh trump is sounding.

Verse 4:
[C]Nations wane, though proud and stately;
[G]Christ His kingdom hasteneth greatly;
[C]Earth her latest pangs is summing;
Shout, ye saints, your Lord is coming.

Verse 5:
[C]Sinners, come, while Christ is pleading;
[G]Now for you He's interceding;
[C]Haste, ere grace and time diminished
Shall proclaim the mystery finished.
